# Lab Overview

## Purpose

This project demonstrates how Active Directory environments can be monitored and defended against common attack techniques.

The focus of this project is not Active Directory administration, but rather the role of a SOC analyst responsible for detecting suspicious authentication activity, identifying attack patterns, and responding to security incidents.

---

## Lab Objectives

- Understand how Active Directory authentication works.
- Identify common attack techniques targeting Active Directory.
- Learn which Windows Event IDs are useful during investigations.
- Design practical detection logic for enterprise environments.
- Practice incident response decision making.

---

## Technologies

- Windows Active Directory
- Windows Event Logs
- Sigma Rules
- MITRE ATT&CK
- Microsoft Security Logging

